/**
 * THE RUN HEARTS — six states.
 *
 * `heart-wagered` carries five paths because the sword is held off the heart by
 * a dark gap. That gap is what keeps both shapes legible when the glyph is one
 * flat colour, and it is why the sword is separate parts rather than a union.
 *
 * A NOTE ON THE CROP, because the lint could not catch it. The tracing step
 * squares each glyph before potrace sees it, and the first version used
 * ImageMagick's `-extent 1:1`. That does not pad to a square — it CROPS to the
 * smaller dimension. The two widest glyphs, the tilted-apart broken heart and
 * the diagonal sword, silently lost their edges, and everything still
 * validated, because a clipped heart is still a centred heart of the right
 * size. Only looking at it caught it. The pipeline now extents to `max(w,h)`.
 */
