/**
 * THE BOTTOM TABS, in two states.
 *
 * `nav-*` is the filled artwork and `nav-*-idle` is the outlined one, which is
 * how this set keeps the convention `TabIcon` argues for: hollow when
 * inactive, solid when active. Sleeper signals the active tab by tint alone,
 * and tint is the one signal that does not survive greyscale or a colour-blind
 * reader — so the shape carries it too.
 *
 * Two artworks rather than one glyph with a stroke mode, because an outline
 * generated as its own drawing keeps an even weight; stroking a filled
 * silhouette of 200+ points produces a tangle at 24pt.
 */
